{% comment %}
  Centralized icon lookup for the booking flow, matching the real theme's
  kerala-ayurveda-icons.liquid pattern — one snippet, icons looked up by name,
  so a repeated icon (like the arrow) isn't pasted separately everywhere it's used.

  Accepts:
  - icon_name: {String} Icon name
  - class: {String} Optional class to add to the svg

  Usage:
  {% render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'arrow-right' %}
{% endcomment %}

{% case icon_name %}
  {% when 'calendar' %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Stethoscope glyph, used for the "Book a consultation" option card.
      Sits inside a translucent white "Overlay" (48x48, rgba(250,250,249,0.15),
      12px radius) per the Figma spec — the same treatment the old calendar
      icon used, so it reads on the dark primary card instead of the raw
      export's own solid light-grey square.

      Icon paths are the export's own, but their tight bounding box is
      only ~13x13 units — centering that via a plain +6/+6 translate left
      the glyph looking noticeably smaller than the Figma reference, where
      it reads as a proper 28px icon inside the 48px circle (explicit
      instruction: "stethoscope icon looks small in ui but large in
      figma"). Scaled up ~2.1x around the glyph's own center (17.646,18),
      then re-centered on the 48x48 frame's center (24,24), instead of
      just increasing the translate — a plain bigger offset alone
      wouldn't have made the glyph itself any bigger, only moved it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="{{ class }}">
      <rect width="48" height="48" rx="12" fill="#FAFAF9" fill-opacity="0.15"/>
      <g transform="translate(24 24) scale(2.1) translate(-17.646 -18)">
        <path d="M14.1042 11.9795H12.6875C12.2963 11.9795 11.9792 12.2966 11.9792 12.6878V15.167C11.9792 17.3186 13.7234 19.0628 15.875 19.0628C18.0266 19.0628 19.7708 17.3186 19.7708 15.167V12.6878C19.7708 12.2966 19.4537 11.9795 19.0625 11.9795H17.6458" stroke="#FAFAF9" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M22.6042 20.4792V21.3646C22.6042 23.2228 21.0978 24.7292 19.2396 24.7292C17.3813 24.7292 15.875 23.2228 15.875 21.3646V19.0625" stroke="#FAFAF9" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M17.6458 11.2705V12.6872" stroke="#FAFAF9" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M14.1042 11.2705V12.6872" stroke="#FAFAF9" stroke-width="1.25" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M24.0208 19.0622C24.0208 19.8446 23.3866 20.4788 22.6042 20.4788C21.8217 20.4788 21.1875 19.8446 21.1875 19.0622C21.1875 18.2797 21.8217 17.6455 22.6042 17.6455C23.3866 17.6455 24.0208 18.2797 24.0208 19.0622Z" stroke="#FAFAF9" stroke-width="1.25"/>
      </g>
    </svg>

  {% when 'monitor' %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Leaf/plant glyph, used for the "Request a therapy session" option card.
      Sits inside a translucent mint "Background" (48x48, rgba(228,242,235,0.5),
      12px radius) per the Figma spec — same treatment style as the stethoscope
      icon's overlay, just mint instead of white since this card is white/light
      rather than dark. Icon fill switched from white to dark green (#00503A,
      matching the original monitor icon's stroke color) so it reads against
      the light background. Original Figma export used an alpha mask to bound
      the path to its 24x24 icon area; dropped here since the path already
      sits fully inside that area on its own — a plain filled path avoids
      introducing a mask id that would be duplicated in the DOM (this icon
      renders twice: mobile + desktop).

      Path's own tight bounding box is ~18.7x17.8 units — checked against
      the stethoscope icon's fix above (same "looks small" complaint):
      this one was already closer to the Figma proportions (~39% fill of
      the 48x48 frame vs the stethoscope's original ~27%) but still short
      of the ~58% fill a real 28px icon in a 48px circle should have, and
      noticeably smaller side-by-side with the now-fixed stethoscope.
      Scaled up 1.5x around the glyph's own center (18.057,18.506), then
      re-centered on the 48x48 frame's center (24,24), same technique as
      the stethoscope fix, so both entry-screen icons read at a
      consistent size again.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="{{ class }}">
      <rect width="48" height="48" rx="12" fill="#E4F2EB" fill-opacity="0.5"/>
