  {%- comment -%}
    Country-code flags for the Patient Details phone field — one inline SVG
    per country in COUNTRY_PHONE_OPTIONS (see the CMS's own
    app/lib/phone-validation.ts, the single source of truth this list is
    deliberately kept in sync with, not the real theme's more limited
    3-country form).

    Each flag's markup is the REAL, official file from Wikimedia Commons
    (the same public-domain source virtually every flag-icon library draws
    from), fetched directly rather than hand-drawn — getting a national
    flag's proportions/colors/star-count wrong is the kind of mistake
    that's easy to make from memory and very visible once made. No library
    dependency was added; this is a one-time content pull, same as every
    other icon in this file being hand-placed markup, not a package.

    Each flag keeps its own REAL viewBox from the source file rather than
    being forced into one shared viewBox — they're genuinely different
    aspect ratios (India/Singapore/Japan ~3:2, UK ~5:3, Germany 5:3,
    UAE/Malaysia/Australia 2:1), so squashing them into a single ratio
    would distort the flag. No width/height attribute is set here, unlike
    this file's other icons — let the .kal-phone-input__flag /
    .kal-country-picker__flag CSS size the container per flag's own
    aspect ratio instead of baking in one fixed size that doesn't fit all
    nine.
  {%- endcomment -%}

